```text
cd ooda
./oodac/oodac check fixtures/residual_macro_fail.oo
  # ERR residual … AST_MACROS
./oodac/oodac emit-c fixtures/residual_macro_fail.oo
  # ERR c_emit unknown free call needs annotation macro_expand
./oodac/oodac tokens fixtures/residual_macro_fail.oo
  # IDENT macro_expand  … STRING  (no splice)
bash scripts/residual_path_a_floor_smoke.oo
  # PASSED (includes residual_macro_fail)
# ephemeral matrix: /tmp/s28_sec_vXJN1s
# IMP1/IMP2: import + SECRET → dual-path ERR secret
# A1e C: f(oo_str_lit("println(token)")) ; gcc: undeclared macro_expand
# I1 emit: oo_print_str(oo_str_lit("${token}"))
```

Close criteria if AST_MACROS ever ships (not this audit):

1. Expand **before** secret walk, **or** walk again on expanded toks.
2. Macro bodies that mention sealed sinks inherit call-site SECRET.
3. Stringify / paste / `${}` of a SECRET IDENT still refuse at sinks.
4. Residual-deny removed only after (1)–(3) have rails.
5. Still **no** claim of full IFC.

